From: xa9igor <32750511+xa9igor@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 23:20:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia: restore RMAPI_GPU_LOCK_INTERNAL on golden image
 channel cleanup

kgraphicsCreateGoldenImageChannel_IMPL() drops the GPU lock and switches
pRmApi to RMAPI_API_LOCK_INTERNAL while it allocates the channel. The
success path re-acquires the GPU lock and switches pRmApi back, but the
error path under cleanup: only re-acquires the lock.

pRmApi->Free() then runs with the GPU lock held through the API-lock
interface: serverResLock_Prologue() asserts and returns
NV_ERR_INVALID_LOCK_STATE, the resource is never removed from
pendingFreeList, and serverFreeResourceTreeUnderLock() spins forever in
the kernel. Seen on S4 resume when the channel allocation fails with
NV_ERR_STATE_IN_USE from GSP (upstream issue 1497, PR 1498).

Switch pRmApi back to RMAPI_GPU_LOCK_INTERNAL when re-acquiring the lock.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/nvidia/src/kernel/gpu/gr/kernel_graphics.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/nvidia/src/kernel/gpu/gr/kernel_graphics.c b/src/nvidia/src/kernel/gpu/gr/kernel_graphics.c
index a2a2c9c4..0a182805 100644
--- a/src/nvidia/src/kernel/gpu/gr/kernel_graphics.c
+++ b/src/nvidia/src/kernel/gpu/gr/kernel_graphics.c
@@ -2559,6 +2559,7 @@ cleanup:
     {
         NV_ASSERT_OK_OR_CAPTURE_FIRST_ERROR(status,
             rmGpuLocksAcquire(GPUS_LOCK_FLAGS_NONE, RM_LOCK_MODULES_GR));
+        pRmApi = rmapiGetInterface(RMAPI_GPU_LOCK_INTERNAL);
     }
 
     if (pVaParams != NULL)
